  "body": "Two follow-ups from the live-log review, both demo-only (no framework counterpart; the Spreadsheet has neither subsystem):\n\n**#1 \u2014 `wantsBodyChange` false-positive.** The correction gate fired when the MIND merely *described* its abilities (\"I can morph my interface\", answering \"what can you do?\") because the bare verb `morph` matched. Tightened to **completed-action phrasing only** (`morphed`, `added a module`, `updated the layout`, \u2026). *Verified:* \"I can morph/add/update\" \u2192 no correction; \"I morphed / added a module / updated the layout\" \u2192 still corrected.\n\n**#3 \u2014 MRI cried wolf on healthy memory.** The immune scan flagged an anomaly whenever `maxX > 50 && maxY > 50` (an **absolute** DFT-magnitude threshold), but a 16-sample luminance DFT clears 50 the instant the picture-memory fills with normal dense data \u2014 so every healthy cube read `\u26a0 anomaly`. Replaced with a **statistical outlier**: a Hofstadter-Cross anomaly now requires a periodic peak towering **>8\u00d7 over the band's own median baseline on both axes** (median is immune to the peak inflating its own threshold). CRC errors remain a hard anomaly. *Verified:* normal dense memory \u2192 clean; an injected period-8 sinusoid \u2192 flagged; a single-axis blip \u2192 clean.\n\n**#2 \u2014 verification pass (no code change).** The **real encrypted save/load path** (`saveCrystalBlob`/`loadCrystalBlob`) round-trips the full Body genome \u2014 primer, immunization, genesis key, scheduled pulses all survive \u2014 confirming the persistence fix end-to-end.\n\n`ORGAN_ATLAS` (\"scanAll/MRI\") and the visual guide (\"2D FFT band scan \u00b7 Hofstadter Cross detection\") remain accurate.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
